  Base LLM provider interface. Concrete implementations (OpenAI, Anthropic) mutate this type.

---

"Provider(url: str, model: str, token: str | None = None)":
  location: provider.py
  annotations: |
    Base LLM provider interface.

    `url`: base API endpoint URL of the provider (exclude version from the URL path).
    `model`: model identifier (e.g. "gpt-4", "claude-3-sonnet", "llama3").
    `token`: API authorization key. Optional — Ollama does not require authentication.
  properties:
    url -> str: |
      Base API endpoint URL of the provider (exclude version from the URL path).
    model -> str: |
      Model identifier.
    token -> str | None: |
      API authorization key. Optional.
  methods:
    "generate(prompt: str) -> answer:str": |
      The generate method produces a response from the LLM based on the provided prompt.

      `prompt`: full prompt text including system instruction and context.
      `answer`: generated response text returned by the LLM.

